 "measures": [
  {
   "name": "Public Measure LY: County Jail Bond (60% required)",
   "jurisdiction": "Johnson County (countywide)",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall the County of Johnson, State of Iowa, issue its general obligation bonds in an amount not exceeding the amount of $94,500,000 for the purpose of acquiring land and constructing, equipping and furnishing a new sheriff’s office and jail facility?"
  },
  {
   "name": "Public Measure LZ: City of Hills Bond (60% required)",
   "jurisdiction": "City of Hills",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall the City of Hills, in Johnson County, State of Iowa, enter into a loan agreement and issue general obligation bonds in an amount not exceeding $5,100,000 for the purpose of paying the cost, to that extent, of constructing furnishing and equipping a municipal building, including fire protection and city hall functionalities?"
  },
  {
   "name": "Public Measure MA: Lone Tree Community School District Bond (60% required)",
   "jurisdiction": "Lone Tree Community School District",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall the Board of Directors of the Lone Tree Community School District in the Counties of Johnson and Louisa, State of Iowa, be authorized to contract indebtedness and issue General Obligation Bonds in an amount not to exceed $6,900,000 to provide funds to remodel, repair, and improve the school building for energy efficiency, including HVAC, mechanical, electrical, and site improvements?"
  },
  {
   "name": "Public Measure VF: Mid-Prairie Community School District Bond (60% required)",
   "jurisdiction": "Mid-Prairie Community School District",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall the Board of Directors of the Mid-Prairie Community School District in the Counties of Washington, Iowa, and Johnson, State of Iowa, be authorized to contract indebtedness and issue General Obligation Bonds in an amount not to exceed $19,000,000 to provide funds to build, furnish, and equip an addition to the high school, including a new events entrance, auditorium, and fine arts classrooms, with related remodeling and improvements and related site improvements; and to renovate, improve, furnish and equip several existing special education and general education classrooms?"
  },
  {
   "name": "Public Measure NC: Kirkwood Community College bond (60% required)",
   "jurisdiction": "Kirkwood Community College (Merged Area X)",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall Kirkwood Community College (Merged Area X) in the Counties of Benton, Black Hawk, Buchanan, Cedar, Clinton, Delaware, Dubuque, Iowa, Jackson, Jefferson, Johnson, Jones, Keokuk, Linn, Louisa, Poweshiek, Tama, and Washington, be authorized to renovate, improve, erect, and equip facilities to modernize learning spaces with an emphasis on health sciences, industrial technologies, agricultural sciences, and business and information technology, contract indebtedness therefor, and issue General Obligation Bonds in an amount not exceeding $88,000,000 for those purposes?"
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Source is the Johnson County Auditor's official 2026 General Election page ('Offices and Issues To Appear On Ballot and Lists of Candidates'); per-precinct sample ballots are only available via an interactive lookup and were not used. Supervisor seats are BY DISTRICT (new under SF 75, 2025): all five districts are up; voters vote only in their own district. Districts 2, 3, 4 are two-year terms; Districts 1 and 5 four-year terms. Township offices: blank entries on the auditor list (empty candidate arrays) mean no candidate filed. Penn and Jefferson townships elect three trustees; Clear Creek trustee vacancy is two seats. West Lucas Trustee lists two candidates (Casey Williams, Wayne Barnes) for one seat as printed. SWCD: three candidates for two seats. Name 'Joel Schillerstron' (Fremont Trustee) copied as printed. No hospital trustee race listed."
}